{"app":"spr-flow","version":3,"nodes":[{"id":"note","type":"info","position":{"x":-806,"y":-496},"data":{"title":"Bound state in the continuum, anisotropic defect (Pankin et al. 2022)","text":"A 1D photonic crystal in air: 20 periods on each side of an anisotropic layer (n_o = 1, n_e = 2, optic axis along x, 125 nm) and an isotropic one (n = 1, 250 nm) — the model of P. S. Pankin et al., J. Opt. Soc. Am. B 39, 968 (2022). x-polarized light sees a Bragg mirror (a gap around 1 µm); y-polarized light a uniform medium: a continuum of waves passing through.\n\nThe defect is the same anisotropic material, L thick, with its optic axis turned by φ = 45°: its localized x-like mode couples to the y continuum and appears as a Fano line in the reflection of y-polarized light (TE here). When the defect is a full-wave plate, (n_e − n_o) L = λ, the leakage cancels: a bound state in the continuum at L = 1 µm, λ = 1 µm, for any φ. The map R(λ, L) shows the line narrowing and vanishing there; its width grows as (L − 1 µm)².","color":"#8a93a6","width":440,"height":310}},{"id":"air","type":"material","position":{"x":-390,"y":-142},"data":{"materialId":"Air","color":"#f4f6fa","indexMode":"absolute","porosity":{"$num":"NaN"}}},{"id":"m1","type":"material","position":{"x":-806,"y":142},"data":{"materialId":"user-pankin-1","color":"#cfe3f2","indexMode":"absolute","porosity":{"$num":"NaN"}}},{"id":"m2","type":"material","position":{"x":-806,"y":354},"data":{"materialId":"user-pankin-2","color":"#7d4fb3","indexMode":"absolute","porosity":{"$num":"NaN"}}},{"id":"arm","type":"aniso","position":{"x":-390,"y":71},"data":{"name":"Arm layer (axis x)","kind":"uniaxial","color":"#7d4fb3","angles":[0,0,0]}},{"id":"def","type":"aniso","position":{"x":-390,"y":496},"data":{"name":"Defect (axis at φ)","kind":"uniaxial","color":"#c24fbd","angles":[0,45,0]}},{"id":"lsw","type":"sweep","position":{"x":-390,"y":944},"data":{"name":"L","kind":"number","mode":"range","min":900,"max":1100,"step":5,"list":""}},